---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const p='/equipment/08-03/',ds='https://www.epfl.ch/research/facilities/cmi/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/DataSheet_5630i_EN_02.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="56i automatic wedge bonder" subtitle="" wide={true} description="Verify the geometry and net edges of an inert wedge-wire bonding program."><script is:inline>window.bondModule=import('/equipment/08-03/bench.mjs');</script><article class="equipment" id="wedge"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/08-03/">← Equipment 08-03</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#bond-refs">References</a><a href="#bond-proof">Verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">08-03 / MICROELECTRONIC ASSEMBLY</p><h2>Two wires planned. One can land.</h2><p class="eq-lede">Run the four-pad coupon on a 5630i thin-wire wedge head. One loop clears the fixture. The other hits a tab and must not become an electrical edge. Raise the loop and rerun to clear the tab.</p></header>
<div class="cols"><section><p class="eq-meta">01 / WORKSTATION</p><h3>F&amp;S Bondtec 56i</h3><div id="bw-view" aria-label="Interactive 5630i assembly and working bay"></div><small id="bw-model" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</small><div class="tools">{[['full','Whole station'],['stage','Workholder'],['coupon','Coupon detail'],['rear','Rear I/O']].map(([k,t])=><button id={'bw-'+k}>{t}</button>)}</div><p>Drag to orbit, scroll or pinch to zoom. Select the workholder, wedge head or display for seating, alignment or program evaluation. The installed tool and accepted wire paths have metric physical scale; use the close-up for the 25 µm wires.</p></section>
<section><p class="eq-meta">02 / PROGRAM</p><h3>Fiducials and clearance</h3><div class="tools"><button id="bw-seat">Unseat coupon</button><button id="bw-align">Apply fiducials</button></div><p id="bw-flags"></p><label>Loop rise above endpoint interpolation (µm)<input id="bw-height" type="number" value="120" min="40" max="2000" step="any"/></label><div class="tools"><button id="bw-run" class="run">Evaluate program</button><button id="bw-raise">Set 500 µm loop</button><button id="bw-reset">Reset example</button></div><p id="bw-status" role="status">Example seated and aligned.</p><details><summary>Work with a custom pad list</summary><p>Load a program with stable pad IDs, intended endpoint pairs, net labels, fiducials and fixture boxes. A new file invalidates alignment. <a href={p+'program.json'} download>Download example input</a>.</p><label>Program JSON<input id="bw-file" type="file" accept=".json,application/json"/></label></details></section></div>
<section><p class="eq-meta">03 / OUTPUT</p><h3>Accepted physical paths and connectivity</h3><p id="bw-result" aria-live="polite"></p><canvas id="bw-plot" width="640" height="270" aria-label="Plan view of pads, keep-outs and accepted/rejected paths"></canvas><p>Gold islands are pads. Teal traces are accepted; dashed copper is the rejected attempted path. The plan view shows XY only; geometry checks include Z and wire radius.</p><div class="over"><table><thead><tr><th>Wire ID</th><th>Physical endpoints</th><th>Net or rejection</th></tr></thead><tbody id="bw-rows"></tbody></table></div><button id="bw-save" disabled>Export assembly JSON</button></section>
<section id="bond-refs"><p class="eq-meta">04 / REFERENCE</p><h3>Documented original configuration</h3><p>The <a href="https://www.epfl.ch/research/facilities/cmi/equipment/packaging-miscellaneous/fs-bondtec-56i-automatic-wire-bonder/">EPFL CMi 56i installation</a> links the <a href={ds+'#page=1'}>manufacturer 5630i wedge-wedge photograph and head diagram, p. 1</a>. The original model follows the white 5600i base, scarlet thin-wire head, separate display, camera and accessible working bay. Undocumented rear port placement, mounts, clamps and enclosure details are inferred, not measured. No reference photos are republished.</p><div class="over"><table><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Documented value / use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Chassis nominal W × D × H</th><td>700 × 650 × 700 mm; external display not in chassis bounds. <a href={ds+'#page=2'}>Datasheet p. 2</a></td></tr><tr><th>Working limits</th><td>100 × 100 mm programmable XY area, 60 mm Z stroke. <a href={ds+'#page=1'}>Datasheet p. 1</a></td></tr><tr><th>Standard wedge / wire</th><td>25.4 mm wedge, 45° standard feed; 25 µm aluminum selected from specified 12.5–75 µm family. The nominal 100 kHz ultrasonic generator is not simulated. <a href={ds+'#page=1'}>Datasheet p. 1</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="tools"><a href={p+'build-model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a><a href={p+'bondtec-5630i.glb'} download>Download GLB</a><a href={p+'xr.json'}>Geometry and VR targets</a><a href={p+'bench.mjs'}>Solver / action module</a><a href={p+'example-assembly.json'}>Example assembly</a></div><small>Metres, named bounds and DOM-free actions support reuse in a VR workshop. This page is desktop/mobile orbit, not a tested headset experience.</small></section>
<section id="bond-proof"><p class="eq-meta">05 / METHOD</p><h3>Clearance is independent of continuity</h3><p>Design XY rotates by θ and then translates by fiducial offset in the machine frame. Pad heights are unchanged. For normalized position u, the loop interpolates the endpoints and adds 4hu(1−u) vertically. The simulator evaluates a 32-segment centreline against each axis-aligned fixture box expanded by 12.5 µm on all faces, a conservative radius test at box corners. A net edge exists only for a safe path and two matching declared nets.</p><div class="over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Verified</th><th>Criterion</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>120 µm, four-pad program</th><td>W1 accepted; W2 hits FRAME_TAB</td><td>W1 accepted; W2 rejected</td><td>Exact ID and endpoint set</td></tr><tr><th>500 µm control</th><td>Both clear</td><td>Two accepted edges</td><td>Exact count</td></tr><tr><th>90° fiducial + (20,30) µm</th><td>D1 at (+2220, −3470) µm</td><td>(+2220, −3470) µm</td><td>±10⁻¹⁰ µm</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p><b>Contract:</b> <code>bts.wedge-program.v1</code> takes 2–60 pads, 1–30 planned bonds, fixed keep-outs, units µm, assembly identity and revision. Outputs <code>bts.bond-assembly.v1</code> with workholder coordinates, ordered ends, centreline vertices, accepted-only net edges, full rejection reasons and parent revision. No force, ultrasonic recipes, wire deformation, sag, tool-body/other-wire collisions, pull strength or quantified production placement accuracy. Numerical checks test planning only; no hardware or reliability certification. A compatible consumer can use the example assembly rather than inferring a short from a rejected path.</p></section>
</article></Layout><script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/08-03/client.mjs';</script><style is:global>
#wedge .cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.15fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:.8rem}#wedge section{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:1rem;margin:.9rem 0;min-width:0}#wedge .cols section{margin:0}#wedge h3{margin:.35rem 0 .6rem;font-size:1.5rem}#wedge .eq-meta{margin:0}#wedge .tools{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:.48rem;margin:.65rem 0}#wedge label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.23rem}#wedge button,#wedge input{min-height:40px;font:inherit;padding:.35rem;box-sizing:border-box;max-width:100%;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--panel,transparent);color:var(--text)}#wedge button{cursor:pointer}#wedge button.run{background:#335b55;color:white}#wedge button:disabled{opacity:.45}#bw-view{height:clamp(270px,33vw,410px);background:#28343a}#bw-view canvas{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;touch-action:none}#bw-plot{width:min(100%,740px);height:auto;display:block}#wedge .over{overflow:auto}#wedge table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}#wedge th,#wedge td{text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.4rem}#bw-result{font-weight:bold}#wedge code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:760px){#wedge .cols{grid-template-columns:1fr}#wedge section{padding:.7rem}}
</style>
